  "justiceSays": [
    {
      "day": 11,
      "line": "📖 Jesse is walking Jorge through a huge smooth white ball sitting on the ground, sometimes head-sized — leaf, stem, smell, the beginner's tour."
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "line": "📖 Jesse is walking Roman through a huge smooth white ball sitting on the ground, sometimes head-sized — leaf, stem, smell, the beginner's tour."
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "line": "They're named, every one: Malik Kowalski, Ellis Khan. Your move — ask them questions (up to three), call a MOOT on it, or turn them away at the edge of the firelight."
    },
    {
      "day": 30,
      "line": "They waited three days at the edge of your fire. Nobody called the moot. Malik nods — not angry, just done — and they walk."
    },
    {
      "day": 34,
      "line": "They're named, every one: Maya Okafor, Grace Ford. Your move — ask them questions (up to three), call a MOOT on it, or turn them away at the edge of the firelight."
    },
    {
      "day": 37,
      "line": "They waited three days at the edge of your fire. Nobody called the moot. Maya nods — not angry, just done — and they walk."
    },
    {
      "day": 46,
      "line": "Emberhold watches to see if Haven holds without its dead. The bond is young — they're still deciding what Haven is, and grief delays the verdict. They'll test the link — count on it, unless Haven answers first: send grain (1,500 kcal), send a speaker (2 days), or let the silence answer. (Trust -8.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 64,
      "line": "🔥 The fire settles. Maya has been quiet all evening, and now everyone knows why. \"Gavel — I put it down today.\" \"It raises the gavel-head high. The sound-block swings forward as a shield. It names your crime first — a full round before the verdict falls.\" \"It names your crime out loud — a real thing you did. The courtroom goes quiet. The naming IS the wound.\" A beat of silence, then the questions come all at once. Ruby says \"We've been walking past those.\" Jorge breathes \"Say that again — slower.\" Someone at the edge of the light says what everyone's thinking: \"So — what are we calling it?\""
    },
    {
      "day": 64,
      "line": "Harlow leans in, voice low. \"Here's what we figured out about Lockpick. Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 64,
      "line": "💡 COUNTER LEARNED — Lockpick: Buy it off. It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase. (Someone at the haven knew the trick.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 64,
      "line": "📓 Codex: Counter: Buy it off — It steals FIRST and fights second — but it CANNOT resist food. OFFER FOOD in the fight: it drops your things mid-scamper for the meal. A bribe is cheaper than a chase."
    },
    {
      "day": 64,
      "line": "★ IDENTIFIED: Wild Ramps. Broad smooth leaves, onion smell. Spring only. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."
    },
    {
      "day": 125,
      "line": "Travel 2 tiles to trail edge.\n— An old trail —\nThe trail is worn smooth as an old coin. Deer, probably. Probably."
    }
  ],
